The issue is that your sidebar has a fixed width of 280px, but the main content margin doesn't account for pages that might need extra space or have content that extends beyond the viewport. Here's the fix:

CSS Fix - Update your main content styles:

Add these CSS rules to your existing <style> section:

```css
/* Fix for main content being covered by sidebar */
.main-content {
    margin-left: var(--sidebar-width);
    padding: 30px;
    transition: var(--transition);
    min-height: 100vh;
    width: calc(100% - var(--sidebar-width));
    max-width: calc(100% - var(--sidebar-width));
    overflow-x: auto;
}

/* Ensure content sections don't get cut off */
.content-section {
    display: none;
    animation: fadeIn 0.5s ease;
    width: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
}

/* Make tables responsive */
.table-responsive {
    overflow-x: auto;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
}

/* Fix for card containers */
.card {
    margin-bottom: 25px;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 5px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
    transition: var(--transition);
    width: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
}

/* Fix for map containers */
.map-container {
    height: 300px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
}

/* Fix for forms */
form {
    width: 100%;
    overflow-x: auto;
}

/* Fix for row containers */
.row {
    margin-left: 0;
    margin-right: 0;
    width: 100%;
}

/* Fix for col containers */
[class*="col-"] {
    padding-left: 15px;
    padding-right: 15px;
}

/* Mobile responsive fix */
@media (max-width: 992px) {
    .main-content {
        width: calc(100% - 70px);
        max-width: calc(100% - 70px);
    }
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
    .main-content {
        margin-left: 0;
        margin-bottom: 70px;
        padding: 15px;
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 100%;
    }
}
```

Additional JavaScript Fix

Add this function to ensure all pages properly handle their layout when switching sections:

```javascript
// Add this function to ensure proper layout when switching pages
function ensureProperLayout() {
    // Force a reflow to fix any layout issues
    setTimeout(function() {
        const mainContent = document.querySelector('.main-content');
        if (mainContent) {
            mainContent.style.opacity = '0.99';
            setTimeout(function() {
                mainContent.style.opacity = '1';
            }, 10);
        }
        
        // Trigger window resize event to force any responsive adjustments
        window.dispatchEvent(new Event('resize'));
        
        // Scroll to top of page when changing sections
        window.scrollTo({ top: 0, behavior: 'smooth' });
    }, 50);
}

