These fixes will:

1. Ensure the main content area properly calculates its width
2. Add horizontal scrolling for content that might be too wide
3. Force a layout recalculation when switching between pages
4. Scroll to the top when changing sections
5. Make sure all forms and tables are fully visible

The main issue was that some pages (like Projects, Assessments, Species, Maintenance) have wider content (tables with many columns, forms with many fields) that were extending beyond the viewport, making them appear "covered" by the sidebar. The overflow-x properties will add scrollbars when needed so users can scroll horizontally to see all content.
